pseudo-label

# 2026-09-19 (session 18): first fire - fold 0 with SGMC pseudo labels, seed 46.
#
# WHY: the scored faults are NEW (rules 1.1/3.3), so the labels are a lower bound on the
# truth and external fault catalogues are the only allowed extra signal (problem page
# #external-datasets).  The QFaults transfer attempt was refused on a total overlap with the
# labels; the SGMC proxy's code-2 population (61,664 px of mapped trace the labels do NOT
# contain) is independent of the labels by construction, so this is the only remaining
# external-catalogue route.
#
# WHAT THIS FIRE DOES: trains fold 0 (configs/config_pseudo_labels.yaml = the block-holdout
# config plus the pseudo pixels as training-window label mass, weight 1.0, seed 46 = the
# baseline's seed) and scores the raw probability field on fold 0's HELD-OUT blocks with the
# same policy (floor 0.1, w0), then paired-bootstraps it against the committed no-pseudo
# baseline (data/evidence/block_holdout/fold0_heldout.json: held-out proxy DTI 0.0806
# [0.0586, 0.1021]).  The pseudo model never saw those blocks' pseudo pixels (training
# windows only - src/dataset.py::make_patches), so a gain on the held-out blocks is
# generalisation of the SGMC-mapped fault style, not label leakage.
#
# NO SHIPPING DECISION IS MADE HERE: a pseudo-labelled ensemble reaches the leaderboard only
# through the field-selection gate (docs/FIELD_SELECTION_RULE.md) as a new reblend.yml
# RUN_ID with measured R3.  This fire produces the measurement such an adoption would need.
#
# Parameters: .github/triggers/pseudo-label-params
